WEBVTT

00:00:00.430 --> 00:00:07.520
As we cast our eyes above to the boundless sky, we know

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:15.620
Whatever tomorrow brings, the sun will always shine

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:19.660
So won't you come with me?

00:00:33.670 --> 00:00:36.760
It's almost time for the school bell to ring

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:38.930
And every moment by moment

00:00:38.930 --> 00:00:41.390
I feel more and more like I could fly

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:44.850
This feeling fills my thoughts and sets my heart alight

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:48.270
It's this moment I love most of all

00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:52.940
In my bag I hold all the things I've overcome

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:56.700
And on their wings, I'll fly into the future

00:00:56.700 --> 00:01:01.240
We can do anything, at any time and any place

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:04.710
And no one can stop us even if they try

00:01:04.910 --> 00:01:09.340
From ING and that alone can we proceed

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:13.260
Carrying all our feelings as we go

00:01:13.460 --> 00:01:17.260
Flying with our dreams for all to see

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:23.720
Let's close today's chapter, and start a new page!

00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:37.450
<i>She changed her movements to match up</i>

00:01:37.450 --> 00:01:38.700
<i>with Elle-chan?</i>

00:01:38.830 --> 00:01:40.280
<i>She knows what they're up to?</i>

00:01:43.950 --> 00:01:44.660
<i>How?</i>

00:01:46.540 --> 00:01:48.250
Look over there.

00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:48.870
What is it?

00:01:48.870 --> 00:01:49.880
See?

00:01:49.880 --> 00:01:51.710
Oh, you're right.

00:01:58.260 --> 00:02:00.220
You're spying for Sako, aren't you?

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:02.050
Shame on you!

00:02:02.050 --> 00:02:04.470
I'm not the type of girl who forgets

00:02:04.470 --> 00:02:05.980
when someone does something for me.

00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:08.060
But more importantly...

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:09.850
I'm not the type to forget

00:02:09.850 --> 00:02:12.060
when someone humiliates me.

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:31.170
Sig-chan!

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:35.710
Sig...

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:50.730
What an idiot...

00:02:51.350 --> 00:02:54.770
There's no way I'd stay in the same position forever.

00:03:01.530 --> 00:03:03.620
That's quite a look on you.

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:08.830
Hm? You'll die if you pull that trigger.

00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:14.040
The muzzle of your gun is filled with mud.

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:17.130
If you fire, the barrel will explode and kill you.

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:24.850
Might as well drench your body in mud, too!

00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:28.680
You're just a piece of junk that can't even fire a single shot!

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:35.770
Those gunshots are from Galil...

00:03:35.770 --> 00:03:37.440
She's surprisingly close.

00:03:37.980 --> 00:03:41.200
I might've been playing around for too long...

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:45.700
You can't fire anymore.

00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:48.240
Just forfeit already, you piece of junk.

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:42.420
S-Sensei..

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:43.920
How's Sig-chan?

00:04:46.430 --> 00:04:50.100
She's... a complete mess.

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:51.720
Well, her hair is, anyway.

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:54.770
That bitch! How dare she?!

00:04:54.770 --> 00:04:56.980
I'll never forgive her for this!

00:04:56.980 --> 00:05:00.360
I won't let her get away with doing whatever she wants!

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:02.740
Whatever she wants?

00:05:03.940 --> 00:05:07.950
It's likely that her goal is to take over this school.

00:05:07.950 --> 00:05:09.910
Take over the school?

00:05:09.910 --> 00:05:11.040
What the hell?

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:12.450
This isn't some manga.

00:05:12.450 --> 00:05:13.290
Is she serious?

00:05:13.750 --> 00:05:16.330
I don't know if she's serious or just flat-out crazy.

00:05:16.330 --> 00:05:19.000
But she's been transferring from one school to another,

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:22.210
leaving them devastated in her wake.

00:05:22.210 --> 00:05:24.670
G3-senpai told me all about it.

00:05:24.670 --> 00:05:26.090
No way...

00:05:27.010 --> 00:05:31.930
She does this by taking down the leader of the school.

00:05:31.930 --> 00:05:36.440
In other words, you're her target, Sixteen.

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:41.980
I've never proclaimed myself a leader of anything.

00:05:41.980 --> 00:05:45.320
But I never back down from a fight!

00:05:49.990 --> 00:05:52.200
Why is Elle running point?

00:05:52.200 --> 00:05:54.160
I'm pinned over here!

00:05:56.330 --> 00:05:57.960
Two against one?!

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:04.340
<i>Retreat while laying down covering fire.</i>

00:06:19.140 --> 00:06:20.520
What the hell's with all this mud?

00:06:20.520 --> 00:06:21.360
It's driving me nuts.

00:06:21.730 --> 00:06:23.320
And what's Elle doing?

00:06:23.320 --> 00:06:24.610
There hasn't been an official announcement.

00:06:24.610 --> 00:06:25.900
Which means she hasn't been hit, right?

00:06:27.820 --> 00:06:31.450
I bet that dud's broken down again.

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:40.080
Keep it together, Elle.

00:06:40.670 --> 00:06:44.210
You're... not the only dud out here.

00:06:52.390 --> 00:06:55.680
Galil's been firing at me for a while now,

00:06:55.680 --> 00:06:57.730
but Sako hasn't taken a single shot at me.

00:06:58.980 --> 00:06:59.600
Wait...

00:07:00.230 --> 00:07:02.980
Is she planning to come up behind me to attempt a pincer attack?

00:07:04.020 --> 00:07:07.610
That means I have to charge through the front!

00:07:08.820 --> 00:07:10.320
Unfortunate.

00:07:10.950 --> 00:07:13.570
I'm at the front, too.

00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:18.790
Damn it!

00:07:23.670 --> 00:07:26.130
How unsightly, Sixteen.

00:07:28.920 --> 00:07:31.090
You can no longer fire,

00:07:31.090 --> 00:07:33.220
now that your barrel's stuck in the mud.

00:07:33.590 --> 00:07:36.640
That's very unbecoming of a gun

00:07:36.640 --> 00:07:39.480
that supposedly represents the West.

00:07:40.140 --> 00:07:42.730
Everyone, take a good look!

00:07:42.730 --> 00:07:45.560
This is your leader right here.

00:07:45.560 --> 00:07:47.320
No matter how strong she may be,

00:07:47.320 --> 00:07:48.730
no matter how popular she may be,

00:07:48.730 --> 00:07:51.150
that's only true in this school.

00:07:51.150 --> 00:07:53.610
In reality, she's weak.

00:07:53.610 --> 00:07:56.870
There are stronger guns in the world.

00:07:56.870 --> 00:08:00.580
They are the true leaders.

00:08:02.750 --> 00:08:04.830
What's so funny?

00:08:04.830 --> 00:08:08.460
I thought Sig's story had some holes in it,

00:08:08.460 --> 00:08:11.880
but you're really thinking about trying to take over this school, huh?

00:08:11.880 --> 00:08:14.220
And what if I am?

00:08:14.220 --> 00:08:16.890
Have you got a screw loose?

00:08:16.890 --> 00:08:17.970
I'm not the leader here.

00:08:19.560 --> 00:08:21.600
I'm no leader.

00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:23.850
I'm just a dud.

00:08:25.690 --> 00:08:28.610
I'm the same as Elle.

00:08:28.610 --> 00:08:30.150
I've had my gun jam in front of enemies,

00:08:30.150 --> 00:08:33.110
and I've been unable to shoot many times.

00:08:33.110 --> 00:08:35.740
I thought I'd never be used again.

00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:41.120
The M16 was once believed to be a defective gun.

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:44.120
In the Vietnam War, it had several issues.

00:08:44.120 --> 00:08:46.670
The allies even said it was better to take the AKs

00:08:46.670 --> 00:08:49.130
from the enemy instead of using their own guns.

00:08:51.050 --> 00:08:54.300
But I started to improve myself, little by little

00:08:54.300 --> 00:08:56.590
and started using better gunpowder,

00:08:56.590 --> 00:08:59.390
and now people use me again.

00:09:00.100 --> 00:09:02.140
That's all there is to it.

00:09:02.140 --> 00:09:04.440
What's your point?

00:09:04.440 --> 00:09:06.100
No matter how many faults I have,

00:09:06.100 --> 00:09:08.150
I'll never get anywhere if I don't try.

00:09:08.150 --> 00:09:09.360
Likewise, if you're good,

00:09:09.360 --> 00:09:11.940
but you become complacent,

00:09:11.940 --> 00:09:13.110
you'll eventually get left behind.

00:09:13.110 --> 00:09:18.070
So we're gonna keep fighting and never give up.

00:09:19.070 --> 00:09:21.830
Good job, Elle! Nice!

00:09:23.500 --> 00:09:24.830
Elle-chan!

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:30.750
You think you've won, Sixteen?

00:09:31.300 --> 00:09:33.010
You must be getting dull

00:09:33.010 --> 00:09:35.260
if you're relying on a little dud

00:09:35.260 --> 00:09:37.300
who can't even pull her trigger.

00:09:38.260 --> 00:09:41.100
See for yourself.

00:09:46.140 --> 00:09:47.390
See?

00:09:49.690 --> 00:09:51.150
Are you stu—

00:09:51.150 --> 00:09:52.860
A plastic bag?

00:09:57.280 --> 00:10:00.030
You don't know when to give up, do you?!

00:10:12.710 --> 00:10:15.590
I've won, Sixteen!

00:10:15.590 --> 00:10:17.760
I aced your team!

00:10:20.680 --> 00:10:21.890
<i>Match over!</i>

00:10:21.890 --> 00:10:27.560
<i>The winners are Team Echo: M16A4 and L85A1!</i>

00:10:28.440 --> 00:10:30.600
Wh-What kinda prank are you trying to pull?

00:10:30.600 --> 00:10:32.940
I'm obviously the winner!

00:10:33.400 --> 00:10:34.980
Maybe you should quit complaining

00:10:34.980 --> 00:10:36.440
and look behind you.

00:10:39.400 --> 00:10:42.870
Why's our flag here?

00:10:42.870 --> 00:10:46.620
That's why I said told her "good job".

00:10:48.120 --> 00:10:49.250
There's no way...

00:10:49.870 --> 00:10:52.040
She brought the flag over here?

00:10:54.590 --> 00:10:57.970
I saw that she brought your flag all the way out here,

00:10:57.970 --> 00:11:00.970
and I knew she was unable to fire.

00:11:00.970 --> 00:11:04.810
So I just had to wait for my chance to shoot the flag.

00:11:05.560 --> 00:11:07.720
It turns out that Elle was the one who gave me

00:11:07.720 --> 00:11:09.060
that chance in the end.

00:11:10.600 --> 00:11:11.980
Don't mess with me!

00:11:11.980 --> 00:11:14.610
It's not gonna end like this, you fucking dumbass!

00:11:14.610 --> 00:11:17.280
Try beating me one-on-one!

00:11:23.120 --> 00:11:24.580
Start complaining again

00:11:24.580 --> 00:11:27.330
and I'll shoot your ear off, <i>dumbass</i>.

00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:29.790
That bitch...

00:11:34.130 --> 00:11:39.010
Sixteen-chan never stopped believing that Elle-chan was coming.

00:11:39.010 --> 00:11:40.630
Funko-chan...

00:11:40.630 --> 00:11:44.140
Elle-chan never gave up during the match

00:11:44.140 --> 00:11:46.720
so that she could help Sixteen-chan.

00:11:55.400 --> 00:11:57.480
I'm envious.

00:11:57.480 --> 00:12:01.490
You really are the leader of this school, Sixteen,

00:12:01.900 --> 00:12:05.570
even if you deny it yourself.

00:12:13.580 --> 00:12:16.710
Looks like I won because of you this time.

00:12:16.710 --> 00:12:19.250
I've seen you in a new light, Little Miss Dud.

00:12:26.390 --> 00:12:27.760
Sako-chan!

00:12:29.350 --> 00:12:30.640
Where are you going?

00:12:31.310 --> 00:12:33.600
The loser always leaves the scene.

00:12:33.600 --> 00:12:37.610
I'm not interested in a school I can't rule over.

00:12:37.610 --> 00:12:39.320
Are you going to transfer schools again?

00:12:39.320 --> 00:12:43.150
Oh yeah, I suppose I owe you an apology, Funko-chan.

00:12:59.380 --> 00:13:02.630
I won't give up on you, though.

00:13:02.630 --> 00:13:03.010
Th-That was my first kiss....

00:13:03.010 --> 00:13:05.260
Until next time, then.
Th-That was my first kiss....

00:13:05.260 --> 00:13:06.130
Th-That was my first kiss....

00:13:06.130 --> 00:13:06.180
Bye, now.

00:13:06.180 --> 00:13:06.970
I was planning on saving it for after someone registered me.
Bye, now.

00:13:06.970 --> 00:13:10.890
I was planning on saving it for after someone registered me.

00:13:10.890 --> 00:13:13.890
Huh? My receiver's fixed.

00:13:17.060 --> 00:13:19.980
<i>So, we've reached the calm after the storm,</i>

00:13:19.980 --> 00:13:23.030
<i>and Sako-chan has left the school.</i>

00:13:23.030 --> 00:13:28.030
<i>She left her legacy behind, and Galil-chan stuck around too.</i>

00:13:28.490 --> 00:13:30.160
<i>And for some reason...</i>

00:13:30.910 --> 00:13:32.330
Hey, Sig-chan.

00:13:33.870 --> 00:13:38.380
<i>Sig-chan wouldn't even talk to me for a little while after that.</i>

00:13:38.380 --> 00:13:40.670
Wh-Why?

00:13:59.520 --> 00:14:03.400
Too bad about the tournament.

00:14:03.400 --> 00:14:05.070
Yeah...

00:14:05.070 --> 00:14:06.570
I guess.

00:14:06.570 --> 00:14:08.820
Don't get so depressed.

00:14:08.820 --> 00:14:10.700
There's still next time.

00:14:10.700 --> 00:14:13.490
Yeah. I know.

00:14:13.490 --> 00:14:15.580
Is the teacher still absent?

00:14:19.000 --> 00:14:20.960
What's wrong, Aug?

00:14:22.500 --> 00:14:25.670
He ate something that had expired, and it didn't sit well.

00:14:26.130 --> 00:14:28.340
I wonder if the powder had degraded...

00:14:28.340 --> 00:14:30.680
People don't use gunpowder.

00:14:32.100 --> 00:14:33.680
Funko?

00:14:34.350 --> 00:14:37.680
If you're that worried about it, just go talk to her.

00:14:39.020 --> 00:14:41.900
Jeez, you're not acting like yourself.

00:14:41.900 --> 00:14:43.110
Girls are meant to be courageous!

00:14:43.110 --> 00:14:44.190
Now, go!

00:14:47.190 --> 00:14:50.160
The AUG isn't just a bullpup; it also has a short barrel,

00:14:50.160 --> 00:14:52.410
so it's incredibly maneuverable.

00:14:53.830 --> 00:14:55.910
I wonder if our teacher likes NATO rounds.

00:14:55.910 --> 00:14:57.830
Who knows...

00:14:58.410 --> 00:15:00.330
That was sad...

00:15:00.330 --> 00:15:03.710
You're pretty strong-willed when you're wearing your heavy barrel.

00:15:03.710 --> 00:15:05.000
Oh, I know!

00:15:05.000 --> 00:15:08.260
You should just switch to your heavy barrel.

00:15:08.260 --> 00:15:09.800
I can't.

00:15:09.800 --> 00:15:10.590
Huh?

00:15:11.300 --> 00:15:14.810
I messed up the last time I did that...

00:15:16.060 --> 00:15:19.850
The Steyr AUG can change its barrels, and by doing so,

00:15:19.850 --> 00:15:22.440
it can become a squad automatic weapon.

00:15:23.690 --> 00:15:26.190
Come with me for a moment.

00:15:29.530 --> 00:15:33.160
Ever since then, I've been scared to talk to her.

00:15:33.950 --> 00:15:37.200
I'm pretty sure Funko was the scared one.

00:15:39.000 --> 00:15:42.250
I want to get close to Funko-sama.

00:15:42.250 --> 00:15:43.630
"Sama"?

00:15:43.630 --> 00:15:46.210
She's good friends with Elle,

00:15:46.210 --> 00:15:49.550
who breaks down all the time...

00:15:49.550 --> 00:15:51.760
We're both bullpups, so why...

00:15:51.760 --> 00:15:54.390
Why are we treated so differently?

00:15:55.140 --> 00:15:57.600
I'm so unlucky...

00:15:57.600 --> 00:16:00.930
I'm not sure where to start telling you what's wrong with that...

00:16:00.930 --> 00:16:04.270
Aug, do you really like Funko that much?

00:16:05.520 --> 00:16:07.690
Do you feel like your hammer's going to fire?

00:16:08.780 --> 00:16:10.990
Like your spring might pop off?

00:16:12.530 --> 00:16:13.860
Like your firing pin's

00:16:13.860 --> 00:16:15.410
gonna drive right through your primer—

00:16:17.700 --> 00:16:20.040
Stop it, Tei! You're being so dirty!

00:16:20.040 --> 00:16:21.580
Man...

00:16:21.580 --> 00:16:23.580
This is a problem.

00:16:23.580 --> 00:16:24.920
I've got it!

00:16:24.920 --> 00:16:27.210
If you can't talk to her directly,

00:16:27.210 --> 00:16:30.460
then just have one of Funko's friends introduce you.

00:16:31.000 --> 00:16:32.510
One of her friends?

00:16:53.400 --> 00:16:54.240
Um...

00:16:55.610 --> 00:16:57.780
Oh, what's up, Aug?

00:16:57.780 --> 00:17:00.370
I, uh...

00:17:00.370 --> 00:17:02.450
I have a favor to ask of you...

00:17:02.450 --> 00:17:03.250
What is it?

00:17:03.250 --> 00:17:06.120
Well... it's actually about Funko-sama...

00:17:10.340 --> 00:17:11.340
Well?

00:17:13.220 --> 00:17:14.380
What is it?

00:17:14.380 --> 00:17:15.930
Oh, um, never mind.

00:17:15.930 --> 00:17:19.260
Sounds like she was in a really bad mood.

00:17:19.260 --> 00:17:20.510
Yeah...

00:17:20.510 --> 00:17:22.680
Try a different friend!

00:17:28.270 --> 00:17:30.480
Um... Eighteen-chan?

00:17:30.480 --> 00:17:32.110
What is it, Aug-chan?

00:17:32.110 --> 00:17:33.940
I was hoping I could ask something of you...

00:17:33.940 --> 00:17:36.030
Eighteen, let's play!

00:17:36.660 --> 00:17:38.990
Hold on a second, Galil-chan.

00:17:38.990 --> 00:17:40.780
I have to talk to Aug-chan about something.

00:17:40.780 --> 00:17:43.290
Okay, I hear ya.

00:17:43.870 --> 00:17:45.080
Sorry about that.

00:17:45.080 --> 00:17:47.500
Ever since the tournament, she's been rather fond of me.

00:17:47.500 --> 00:17:49.040
No, it's fine.

00:17:49.040 --> 00:17:50.500
Anyway...

00:17:50.500 --> 00:17:52.500
Oh, no! Don't do that!

00:17:52.500 --> 00:17:53.710
Don't do that, Galil-chan!

00:17:55.130 --> 00:17:56.930
Use a bottle opener.

00:17:56.930 --> 00:17:59.390
If your magazine lip gets bent, it'll cause a jam.

00:17:59.930 --> 00:18:02.350
Thanks! You're so nice, Eighteen.

00:18:06.310 --> 00:18:08.060
Sorry about that.

00:18:08.060 --> 00:18:09.900
That's Galil.

00:18:12.650 --> 00:18:15.610
She's an AR, so she doesn't have a bottle opener.

00:18:15.610 --> 00:18:17.820
But she wanted to open it on her own anyway.

00:18:18.660 --> 00:18:21.320
Um, I see...

00:18:21.320 --> 00:18:24.540
Anyway, what did you want to talk about?

00:18:24.540 --> 00:18:28.670
Well, about that... The thing is, Funko-sama...

00:18:44.430 --> 00:18:47.350
Sometimes the timing just doesn't work out.

00:18:47.350 --> 00:18:48.770
Yeah...

00:18:48.770 --> 00:18:50.730
How about we ask another friend?

00:18:50.730 --> 00:18:53.230
Elle's close to Funko, right?

00:18:54.070 --> 00:18:54.770
Elle...

00:18:55.230 --> 00:18:57.070
You're both bullpups...

00:18:57.070 --> 00:18:59.030
I'm sure she'll help you out.

00:18:59.490 --> 00:19:05.160
But I came out before her, and was successfully adapted first.

00:19:05.160 --> 00:19:07.290
She might not think that well of me.

00:19:07.290 --> 00:19:09.330
That's not true!

00:19:09.330 --> 00:19:11.290
I'm sure she'll understand if you talk to her!

00:19:14.210 --> 00:19:16.710
That is, if you can talk to her.

00:19:16.710 --> 00:19:18.300
She's not here.

00:19:18.760 --> 00:19:21.090
What are you doing here, fountain hair?

00:19:21.090 --> 00:19:22.640
Elle broke again, so she's not here.

00:19:22.640 --> 00:19:24.800
I'm not a fountain!

00:19:24.800 --> 00:19:25.640
Oh, I know.

00:19:25.640 --> 00:19:27.390
Why don't you ask Sixteen?

00:19:27.850 --> 00:19:28.680
Huh?

00:19:30.810 --> 00:19:33.980
If you wanted to talk to Fukko, you should have just said so.

00:19:33.980 --> 00:19:35.900
Did she do something again?

00:19:35.900 --> 00:19:38.440
No, that's not why...

00:19:38.440 --> 00:19:39.490
No, it's fine.

00:19:39.490 --> 00:19:42.490
Fukko's always up to no good.

00:19:42.490 --> 00:19:44.490
Don't hold back. Just give it to her.

00:19:44.490 --> 00:19:45.990
I couldn't possibly do that...

00:19:45.990 --> 00:19:46.660
It's fine.

00:19:47.540 --> 00:19:50.080
You want me to get her to meet you behind the gym?

00:19:50.080 --> 00:19:52.290
N-Not at all.

00:19:52.290 --> 00:19:54.420
What are you doing?

00:19:57.300 --> 00:19:59.460
Oh, it's Tei-chan and Aug-chan.

00:19:59.460 --> 00:20:00.380
You two are always together, huh?

00:20:02.930 --> 00:20:04.970
Come on, Aug. This is your chance.

00:20:04.970 --> 00:20:07.930
Come on. If you've got something to say, just say it.

00:20:19.650 --> 00:20:21.320
What is it, Aug-chan?

00:20:25.870 --> 00:20:27.280
Aug!

00:20:33.750 --> 00:20:37.960
You got hot enough to burn your barrel...

00:20:39.090 --> 00:20:42.670
Wouldn't it have been better to switch to your heavy barrel?

00:20:51.220 --> 00:20:54.350
So, the Japanese teacher said he was going to buy one...

00:20:54.350 --> 00:20:57.020
Elle-chan, you're all better now?

00:20:57.020 --> 00:20:58.480
That's good.

00:20:58.480 --> 00:21:00.820
Try not to break so much.

00:21:06.410 --> 00:21:07.620
What's this?

00:21:09.780 --> 00:21:11.910
These scones look delicious.

00:21:11.910 --> 00:21:13.870
Did you make them, Elle-chan?

00:21:14.710 --> 00:21:16.670
These are for us?

00:21:17.460 --> 00:21:19.290
Thank you, Elle-chan.

00:21:22.550 --> 00:21:24.170
How nice...

00:21:24.170 --> 00:21:26.840
I wish I was a dud, too.

00:21:26.840 --> 00:21:29.850
I think you're pretty much there, to be honest.

00:21:39.770 --> 00:21:41.690
Huh? What?

00:21:41.690 --> 00:21:44.780
I'll teach you how to make scones.

00:21:44.780 --> 00:21:45.900
Scones?

00:21:46.240 --> 00:21:48.200
They'll be good.

00:21:48.200 --> 00:21:50.530
Let's make them together, Aug-chan.

00:21:55.660 --> 00:21:56.620
Yeah!

00:22:00.290 --> 00:22:06.930
Let's tear another page off our calendar

00:22:07.970 --> 00:22:14.470
Together we braved

00:22:18.900 --> 00:22:26.400
past ages and never-ending conflict

00:22:26.690 --> 00:22:34.040
Together we laughed and cried in those hectic times

00:22:34.870 --> 00:22:39.620
When I ran

00:22:42.540 --> 00:22:53.050
I put my footsteps into the ground

00:22:54.100 --> 00:23:00.770
Let's tear another page off our calendar

00:23:01.730 --> 00:23:07.940
Something is bound to change

00:23:09.360 --> 00:23:16.120
One by one the days I tore off pile up

00:23:16.620 --> 00:23:20.000
like a past I cannot erase

00:23:20.460 --> 00:23:26.170
They will be my strength for days to come

00:23:31.010 --> 00:23:31.720
Eighteen here!

00:23:31.720 --> 00:23:33.550
It's New Year's Day next time!

00:23:33.550 --> 00:23:35.350
My parents in Aichi are sending me rice cakes,

00:23:35.350 --> 00:23:36.720
so I'm really excited.

00:23:36.720 --> 00:23:39.930
Next time: Be afraid! Visit! Wrap up!
